.TH UNIM-INDICATOR 1 "July 2026" "UNIM 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-indicator \- UNIM tray indicator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-indicator
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBunim\-indicator\fR is the dedicated system\-tray (StatusNotifier) process
for UNIM (Universal Next\-generation Input Method). It displays the current
input mode (KO/EN), exposes a context menu for mode switching and quick
settings, and follows the desktop dark/light theme automatically.
.PP
In UNIM 0.3.0 the previous monolithic \fBunim-gui\fR GUI binary was split
into three single\-responsibility processes: \fBunim\-indicator\fR (this tray
process), \fBunim\-settings\fR (the libadwaita settings dialog), and
\fBunim\-popup\-service\fR (the popup renderer). All three communicate with
the daemon over the \fBorg.atit.unim.*\fR D\-Bus interfaces.
.PP
The indicator is normally launched on session start via
\fIunim\-indicator.desktop\fR, but it can also be started manually for
debugging.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-daemon
Run in the foreground without daemonizing.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH D\-BUS INTERFACE
.TP
.B Daemon service
org.atit.unim.Daemon
.TP
.B Object path
/org/atit/unim/Daemon
.PP
The indicator subscribes to mode\-change signals and invokes config and
mode\-switch methods on the daemon. It does not expose its own D\-Bus
service \(em it is a pure client.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UNIM_DEVELOP
Set to "1" to enable verbose debug logging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/autostart/unim\-indicator.desktop
Per\-user autostart entry (installed by the desktop integration step).
.TP
.B /usr/share/applications/unim\-indicator.desktop
System\-wide desktop entry.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-daemon (1),
.BR unim\-settings (1),
.BR unim\-popup\-service (1)
